nina: CI started failing for edge-sdk tests after we made the SDK ESM-only. Jest job errors with 'Cannot use import statement outside a module' when loading our __mocks__.

alex: which mock file?

nina: __mocks__/auth.ts — it uses `import { getToken } from '../../src/auth'`. Jest runs as CJS in CI so the static import fails.

yusuf: Vitest handles that because it runs ESM, but we still hit issues with hoisted mocks before esbuild transpile unless we add deps.inline.

alex: Short fixes: 1) convert mock to conditional require for Jest, 2) run edge-suite under Vitest in CI, or 3) add a tiny pretest compile for __mocks__ to CJS. All ugly in different ways.

nina: I tried a conditional mock:
```
// __mocks__/auth.ts
if (typeof jest !== 'undefined') {
  module.exports = { getToken: jest.fn(() => Promise.resolve('tok')) };
} else {
  export const getToken = vi.fn(() => Promise.resolve('tok'));
}
```
works locally but lint/TS hates mixed module style.

yusuf: For typings the workaround is add `allowSyntheticDefaultImports` in tsconfig.test or cast mocks with `as unknown as typeof import('../../src/auth')`. Not ideal but reduces TS noise.

alex: Proposal: add a short DevEx page with canonical examples: Jest(CJS) manual mock, Jest(ESM) config snippet (ts-jest useESM), and Vitest example with deps.inline and esbuild target. Also add a temporary CI job that runs the edge-sdk tests under Vitest so PRs surface these regressions.

ci-bot: CI: workflow #5201 failed on job jest-edge (https://ci.internal/runs/5201).

nina: I'll open INF-1052 to track and prototype the Vitest job. I'll attach a minimal vitest config and one converted test.

yusuf: I can help port helper utils and handle snapshot differences.

alex: I'll write the DevEx doc and include troubleshooting tips for sourcemaps when using ts-jest + useESM.

nina: thanks all — will follow up in INF-1052.
